Spec: Windows ConnectionJournal

Purpose:
  Retain caller-bound formal connection state and one-use attachments.

Owns:
  ./ConnectionJournal.cs

References:
  ./LocalAccess.sdd
  /contracts/dotnet/LinkGate.Contracts/ConnectionStatus.sdd

Must:
  Reuse the local-access authority stamp when retaining a formal connection scope.
  Allow coalesced snapshots to skip forward through pending/attaching/open/draining while rejecting reverse progress; slow half-closed streams must retain observed counters before termination.
  Atomically admit exact local access, normalized request digest, original operation outcome and initial status under schema eight.
  Replay matching old operations before current authority or quota checks without redial; reject changed intent and cross-caller references.
  Keep successful open results after close/restart, but expose failures that occurred before transport readiness.
  Bind single-use attachment claims to caller, original boot and current exact local access; consume each native attachment only once.
  Reject stale or terminal snapshot updates and any identity/path/counter/time regression; recover old active rows in bounded batches with incomplete counters.
  Apply combined experimental/formal active-flow limits and existing durable operation/revocation quotas without eviction.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify state, persistence, replay, recovery and failure boundaries with owned local fixtures.
